  "body": "Part of #1446. Found while working #1489 (PR to follow on that issue).\n\nFixture: a 60 x 40 pocket with 3 mm corners, roughed by a 12 mm tool, then a rest pass with a 4 mm tool (`crates/app/tests/rest_pocket.rs`, `read_against_the_simulated_roughing_pass`). When the rest pass is read against the stock simulation of the roughing pass, each corner ring cuts its corner. But the inner leg of the ring crosses floor that the 12 mm tool already cleared: 6.7 mm of a ring that is 14.8 to 15.3 mm long, at each level. These are feed moves, so they cost time and do not make the cut unsafe.\n\nWanted: in `machining2d::rest_pocket`, the rings over a crescent-shaped rest area do not feed along their inner side over cleared floor. For example, open rings that turn back, or a link that goes up and over the cleared floor. The rest area must stay a superset of the material that is left (Prime Directive, #1446).\n\nDone means: the fixture's measured air length per ring goes down from about 6.7 mm, and the coverage tests in `crates/motion/tests/rest2d.rs` stay green.",
